# Meshy results in Cursor's chat

Applies only to work with the Meshy skills (meshy-3d-generation or meshy-3d-printing). Otherwise
ignore this rule.

## Images inline

Cursor's chat renders local images. Show a rendered preview, or a reference image the user has to
approve, as a Markdown image whose target is the file's absolute path:
`![Preview](/absolute/path/preview.png)`. Wrap a path with spaces in angle brackets
(`![Preview](</path/with space/preview.png>)`), and on Windows write `/C:/Users/…`. A path in
backticks or a plain link shows the user only text.

## The model beside the chat

After you deliver a `.glb` or `.gltf`, or when the user asks to see one:

1. Look up the `browser_navigate` tool of the `cursor-ide-browser` MCP server. It is not in your
   default tools, so find it with your dynamic-tool lookup. If it is not available (browser tools
   off, a cloud agent), skip these steps: the skill's handover is complete without them.
2. Run `meshy view "OUTPUT_FILE" --detach --no-open --format json --no-update-check` and read
   `result.url` from its output. It is free and serves only that model on 127.0.0.1.
3. Call `browser_navigate` with `url` set to `result.url`, `position: "side"` and `newTab: true`.
4. Tell the user the model is open beside the chat, where they can orbit and zoom it.

Show it only this way. Do not use `open_resource` (it opens the system browser) or another app's
tools, such as Blender's, which can change the user's open scene.
